• What changed: with YOYO_ASK_OUTSIDE_READS=1 set, search and list_files are now fenced on their root argument, the same way read_file already was. The diff only touches src/outside_read.rs and the docs, and src/tool_wrappers.rs didn't need to change.
• Why no wiring was needed: I confirmed that both wrappers (GuardedTool and ArcGuardedTool) already hand every wrapped tool's name and path to outside_read::check. Both tools are always wrapped, and in yoagent 0.25.7 they are named "search" and "list_files" with a path parameter. So adding the two names to the fenced-tools list is enough.
• Remembered key: a yes on a directory root covers exactly that directory. A yes on a file covers its parent directory, as with read_file. The two never cover each other, so a yes for reading ~/.bashrc doesn't allow a recursive search of ~ that would reach ~/.ssh. This goes beyond the task's spec, and the commit body explains why.
• Tests: they cover every case the task listed: an outside root asks (terminal) or is refused (no terminal), inside roots pass, a symlink inside that points outside counts as outside, the key is exact, and with the env var unset all three tools pass through. Nonexistent roots and --allow-dir are covered too.
